      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishers_Island%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hurricanes have shaped Fire Island, with the Great September Gale of 1815 and the 1938 New England Hurricane causing widespread damage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishers_Island%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Fire Island Light Station was added to the National Register of Historic Places on September 11, 1981.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/fiis/learn/historyculture/index.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1870, a lifesaving station was erected at the western end of the island by Connecticut, overlooking waters between Fishers Island and Little Gull Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishers_Island%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, a permanent Coast Guard station was built on the west end.",
